course: dictionary
lesson: 13623
title: Polite words for being unwell
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words sound polite and formal, the way grown-ups speak in letters, on the news, or when they do not want to give every detail. Indisposed is one of them. It is a grown-up way of saying someone is not well enough to do something.
explain: «The singer is indisposed tonight.» The singer is not well enough to sing, but the sentence does not say what is wrong. That kind of polite word for a sensitive thing is called a euphemism.
explain: The context helps you. If the show is cancelled or another singer goes on stage, indisposed must mean unwell or unable to take part. Ask yourself: what would fit here? Then try "unwell" in the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Indisposed has a second, very rare meaning. «She is indisposed to help» means she is not willing to help. You will mostly meet this sense in very old or very formal writing, so read the whole sentence before you decide.
fact: Indisposed means slightly ill, so not able to come or work.
fact: Indisposed is formal, and it is often a euphemism, a polite way of not giving the exact reason.
fact: «The singer is indisposed tonight» means the singer is unwell and cannot perform.
fact: Indisposed can also mean not willing to do something, as in «indisposed to help».
fact: The word is rare outside formal writing, so context clues are your best friend.
exercise: «The head teacher is indisposed today, so the assembly is cancelled.» What does indisposed mean? | Busy with a big project | Lost on the way to school | *Slightly ill, so unable to come | Very happy and full of energy
exercise: «Her grandad is indisposed and cannot drive us.» Which word is closest in meaning to indisposed? | angry | strong | cheerful | *unwell
exercise: Priya says indisposed is a type of small dog. Who is correct? | *Priya is wrong, it means slightly ill or unable to come | Priya is right, it means very angry | Priya is wrong, it means very fast | Priya is right, it is a small dog
test: «The chef is indisposed, so the restaurant is closed for lunch.» What is the most likely reason? | The chef is very rich | The chef has lost the keys | *The chef is slightly ill and cannot work | The chef is on holiday in the sun
test: In the sentence «She is indisposed to help», what does the word mean? | Unable to see | Too tired to read | *Not willing to help | Glad to help
exam: «The minister was indisposed, so her deputy gave the speech.» What does indisposed tell you? | She was on a boat | She was happy to give a speech | She had lost her voice forever | *She was slightly ill and could not come
